.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-admin-purchases-refund-taxes - Refund only the Gumroad-collected taxes on a purchase


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad admin purchases refund-taxes  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Refund the Gumroad-collected taxes on a purchase without touching the
purchase price. The buyer email is required as a sanity check against
the purchase record.

.PP
--note records an admin-side note alongside the tax refund. --business-vat-id
attaches a buyer-supplied VAT ID to the refund record (commonly required
when a B2B buyer needs the tax reversed because they self-account for VAT).
--vat-exempt-territory marks the purchase's subscription as belonging to a
buyer in an EU-VAT-exempt territory such as the Canary Islands, so every
future renewal is charged without VAT. Use it when the buyer has no VAT ID
to enter and their checkout connection geolocated to the mainland.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--business-vat-id\fP=""
	Buyer's business VAT ID

.PP
\fB--email\fP=""
	Buyer email (required)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for refund-taxes

.PP
\fB--note\fP=""
	Admin note attached to the tax refund

.PP
\fB--vat-exempt-territory\fP[=false]
	Mark the subscription as an EU-VAT-exempt territory buyer so renewals are charged without VAT


